WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:12.360
December 1944 in the city of Bastogne
Belgium during the Battle of the Bulge

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:17.680
American soldiers primarily from the
hundred and first Airborne Division but

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:25.150
also from the nine 69th artillery
battalion and combat command B of the

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:32.649
tenth Armored Division were surrounded
by Germans they were outnumbered by

00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:41.200
approximately five to one they were
lacking in cold weather gear they were

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:49.720
short on ammunition and low on food and
medical supplies the weather was

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:55.600
horrible
due to heavy cloud cover resupply from

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:06.579
the air was not possible they appeared
to be doomed that is certainly what the

00:01:06.579 --> 00:01:14.740
Germans thought so on the 22nd of
December the Germans sent a message with

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:19.659
two young German officers offering an
opportunity for the Americans to

00:01:19.659 --> 00:01:30.219
surrender the message read to the USA
commander of the encircled town of

00:01:30.219 --> 00:01:40.240
Bastogne the fortune of war is changing
this time the USA forces in and near

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:47.649
Bastogne have been encircled by strong
German armored units more German armored

00:01:47.649 --> 00:01:54.520
units have crossed the river or feu near
or through Ville have taken Marche have

00:01:54.520 --> 00:02:03.880
reached st. who bear by passing through
hombre cebre till a Libra malt is in

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:10.959
German hands there is only one
possibility to save the encircled us a

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:14.549
troops from Total Annihilation

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:22.060
that is honorable surrender of the
encircled town in order to think it over

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:27.190
a term of two hours will be granted
beginning with the presentation of this

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:35.319
note if this proposal should be rejected
one German artillery Corps and six heavy

00:02:35.319 --> 00:02:43.299
AAA battalions are ready to annihilate
the USA troops in and near Bastogne the

00:02:43.299 --> 00:02:49.140
order for firing will be given
immediately after this two hours term

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:56.099
all the serious civilian losses caused
by this artillery fire would not

00:02:56.099 --> 00:03:08.290
correspond with the well-known American
humanity signed the German commander the

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:13.870
American commander General Anthony
McAuliffe upon hearing this offer didn't

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:23.350
like the idea at all in fact his initial
response was simply nuts after a little

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:27.910
discussion with his staff on what the
proper written response would be they

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:36.579
decided that was the proper response so
they put together a formal note on

00:03:36.579 --> 00:03:46.780
letterhead to return to the German
commander it read 22 December 1944 to

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:55.930
the German commander nuts signed the
American commander on Christmas Eve

00:03:55.930 --> 00:04:05.609
general McAuliffe sent out a message to
his troops in the besieged city it read

00:04:05.609 --> 00:04:12.430
headquarters hundred first Airborne
Division the office of the division

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:22.650
commander 24 December 1944 what's merry
about all this you ask

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:32.350
we're fighting it's coal
we aren't home all true but what has the

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:36.400
proud Eagle Division accomplished with
it's worthy comrades of the tenth

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:43.000
Armored Division the 750 ank destroyer
battalion and all the rest just this

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:48.550
we have stopped cold everything that has
been thrown at us from the north east

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:54.610
south and west
we have identifications from four German

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:59.770
Panzer divisions two German infantry
divisions and one German parachute

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:07.060
division these units spearheading the
last desperate German lunge were headed

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:12.070
straight west for key points when the
Eagle Division was hurriedly ordered to

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:19.840
stem the advance how effectively this
was done will be written in history not

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:26.020
alone in our divisions glorious history
but in world history the Germans

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:34.870
actually did surround us their radios
blared our doom their commander demanded

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:42.580
our surrender in the following impudent
arrogance and that's when the general

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:47.380
added in the note of the Germans
surrender demand and he gave his

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:56.440
response the simple response of nuts he
wanted all the troops to know then then

00:05:56.440 --> 00:06:01.270
he closed out the memo explaining their
current situation on the ground the

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:08.680
message continued Allied troops are
counter-attacking in force we continued

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:16.470
to hold Bastogne by holding Bastogne we
assure the success of the Allied armies

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:24.790
we know that our division commander
general Taylor will say well done we are

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:28.210
giving our country and our loved ones at
home

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:33.340
a worthy Christmas present and being
privileged to take part in this gallant

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:37.060
feat of arms are truly making for
ourselves

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:52.600
a Merry Christmas AC McAuliffe well the
Germans did attack Bastogne on Christmas

00:06:52.600 --> 00:07:00.730
Day and they did initially break through
the American perimeter but the American

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:05.500
soldiers stood their ground and defeated
the attack eventually destroying all the

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:13.930
German tanks then the next day the 26th
of December General Patton's 4th Armored

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:18.729
Division along with the 26th Infantry
Division broke through to Bastogne and

00:07:18.729 --> 00:07:27.040
opened up a corridor to relieve the
embattled but victorious troops it was a

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:33.190
glorious example of will and defiance
and undaunted courage in the face of

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:45.600
seemingly insurmountable odds and it was
an example of the victory of light over

00:07:45.600 --> 00:08:02.740
darkness but let us never forget that
for every victory there is a cost there

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:11.919
is sacrifice and one letter home also
written

00:08:11.919 --> 00:08:20.289
on Christmas Eve December 24th 1944 from
the Battle of the Bulge by Lieutenant

00:08:20.289 --> 00:08:29.159
Colonel Arthur Blair the commanding
officer of the 268 Field Artillery

00:08:29.159 --> 00:08:38.709
Battalion who was born in New Orleans
and raised in Mississippi this letter

00:08:38.709 --> 00:08:48.449
shows some of that sacrifice the letter
was written to Colonel Blair's parents

00:08:48.449 --> 00:08:53.709
but in the letter he also speaks of his
young wife Mary and their three-year-old

00:08:53.709 --> 00:09:01.680
daughter Susan this is what he wrote

00:09:04.529 --> 00:09:14.870
dear folks
well so this is Christmas Eve I've spent

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:20.180
a lot of lonely ones those when I've
been away from you and Merry but I've

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:26.240
never spent one quite this lonely and
one in which the Christmas spirit seemed

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:33.050
so lacking in the surroundings even the
first one of the war with Mary leaving

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:39.649
the next day was not so bad as this one
then I had things to worry about and

00:09:39.649 --> 00:09:46.910
lots of work to do but here everything
is as it has been the same day-in

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:52.850
day-out routine and all I have to think
of is how much I miss you and Mary and

00:09:52.850 --> 00:10:01.459
Susie and what fun and how comfortable
and right it would be if we were all

00:10:01.459 --> 00:10:11.800
spending Christmas Eve and Christmas
together we will have turkey tomorrow

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:17.120
then some of the men will have received
Christmas packages and that will be the

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:28.420
extent of our Christmas there is no
peace around us no peace in our hearts

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:40.720
the Christmas star is an airplane flare
the three wisemen where are they now

00:10:41.649 --> 00:10:49.459
there's nothing here but anger in men's
hearts the wisest men are those who do

00:10:49.459 --> 00:10:58.459
the best job of killing the enemy while
avoiding death themselves the main Jers

00:10:58.459 --> 00:11:03.529
are corrupt with dead and rotting cattle
and the village ends gape at the night

00:11:03.529 --> 00:11:17.040
through the glass windows and tireless
roofs the gifts of the Magi are steel

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:32.730
and flame and high explosives but deep
in my heart I know that peace will come

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:39.510
again and families will again be
together for God and his son are

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:49.710
watching over us and protecting us all
as well as we will let them so in the

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:57.230
hope of tomorrow and the peace to come
dear dad and mom merry Christmas to you

00:11:57.230 --> 00:12:11.570
and a happy and peaceful new year all my
love your son Arthur

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:33.710
well Arthur did not make it home to be
with his family again the next day

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:40.620
Christmas 1944 as he was wishing the
officers and men of his battalion and

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:48.090
Merry Christmas a German shell hit
wounding several of the men and killing

00:12:48.090 --> 00:13:01.890
Colonel Arthur W Blair he was one of the
19 thousand Americans killed in the

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:08.640
Battle of the Bulge
in one of the thousands upon thousands

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:24.000
upon thousands that have died for our
flag and the ideals of freedom that it

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.690
represents

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:39.980
colonel Blair's executive officer wrote
a letter to the family and said the

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:45.530
memory of the colonel is one that will
always be kept green by those who knew

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:52.520
him and had served with him he was an
outstandingly gallant officer a fine

00:13:52.520 --> 00:14:01.270
leader and above all else
a true gentleman on the field of battle

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:12.890
where there can be no sham he proved it
beyond the question of a doubt and the

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:20.720
executive officer signed off the letter
quoting Shakespeare when Horatio bid a

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:29.920
final farewell to his friend
Hamlet now cracks a noble heart

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:37.810
goodnight sweet prince and flights of
angels sing thee to thy rest

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:55.130
- all those noble souls that left us too
young and cracked our hearts we bid you

00:14:55.130 --> 00:15:08.600
the same goodbye may flights of angels
sing you to your rest we will remember

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:25.680
you always and we are thinking of you
this holiday season Merry Christmas

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:36.180
and a Happy New Year to all and may
there be peace on earth

